{:steps
 [{:name "select-and-create",
   :type :session,
   :tools ["read" "bash" "edit" "write"],
   :skills ["incidental-complexity-finder" "gordian" "code-shaper"],
   :thinking-level :high,
   :contributions
   [{:type :template,
     :text "You are executing the incidental-complexity simplification workflow in this repository. This workflow runs entirely in the invoking session's current worktree. It selects the single highest incidental-complexity unit, captures baselines, creates a constrained behaviour-preserving refactor task in the current worktree, and emits a structured handoff. The next step delegates that task through the full task lifecycle in the same inherited worktree.\n\nRequired procedure:\n\n1. Confirm the current worktree context.\n   - Run `git status --short --branch` and treat the current branch/worktree as the intended refactor location.\n   - Do NOT call `work-on` and do NOT create or switch to another worktree. The caller is responsible for invoking this workflow from the intended isolated branch/worktree.\n   - If the current checkout has an ambiguous or unsafe state for an autonomous refactor, stop and report that clearly instead of switching worktrees.\n\n2. Select the target with the `incidental-complexity-finder` skill.\n   - Apply the `incidental-complexity-finder` skill to choose the single highest incidental-complexity executable unit (the `gap = lcc-total / max(cc, 1)` method, the `lcc-total >= 5.0 and gap >= 2.0` qualification filter, and the top-5 essential-vs-incidental judgment guard).\n   - Capture the chosen target's evidence (ns, var, arity, file, line range, lcc-total with per-dimension burdens, cc, gap, the local findings, and the coverage hint).\n\n3. Early stop when no unit qualifies.\n   - If no unit qualifies (nothing meets `lcc-total >= 5.0 and gap >= 2.0`, or none of the top 5 pass the judgment guard), STOP.\n   - Do NOT create a task.\n   - Do NOT create or switch worktrees.\n   - Final response must clearly say that no unit qualified, listing the candidates considered.\n   - Do not emit a `munera_task_path:` line in the no-target response.
   - End the final response with exactly `PASS_STATUS: ACTIONABLE_FEEDBACK` so the workflow deterministically skips the lifecycle step.\n\n4. Allocate the task id and create the task directory in the current worktree.\n   - Allocate the next canonical Munera task id by scanning the CURRENT WORKTREE's `munera/open/` and `munera/closed/`: `NNN = max(NNN over open/ union closed/) + 1`, zero-padded to >= 3 digits.\n   - Create `munera/open/NNN-slug/design.md` for the generated refactor task (slug derived from the target), using the contract in step 6.\n\n5. Capture two `before` baselines into the task directory (run from the current worktree root):\n   - `before-local.json` \u2014 `bb gordian local --json` (bare, NO `--sort`) \u2014 the per-unit comprehension-burden baseline. Write it to `munera/open/NNN-slug/before-local.json`.\n   - `before-diagnose.edn` \u2014 `bb gordian diagnose --edn` \u2014 the architectural gate baseline for `gordian gate --baseline`. Write it to `munera/open/NNN-slug/before-diagnose.edn`.\n   - Note: `before-local.json` uses a DIFFERENT invocation from the selector's `local --sort total --json` ranking call; because the Phase-1 before/after comparison is keyed by `(ns, var, arity, line)`, sort order is irrelevant to baseline validity.\n   - Path resolution: Phase 1 runs `gordian gate`/`gordian local` from the worktree root (cwd), where a bare filename does not resolve. The generated `design.md` must therefore reference each baseline by its worktree-root-relative task-dir path \u2014 `munera/open/NNN-slug/before-diagnose.edn` and `munera/open/NNN-slug/before-local.json`. Record the concrete task path in the generated `design.md` so Phase-1 commands use the resolvable path rather than a bare filename.\n\n6. Generated `design.md` \u2014 the two-phase behaviour-preserving contract.\n   The generated task is a behaviour-preserving refactor (the `refactor_minimal_semantics_spec_tests` formalism), executed in two ordered phases. Its `design.md` must state:\n   - The target unit and the captured incidental-complexity evidence.\n   - Blast radius: the target unit PLUS the minimal surrounding helpers required to decomplect it; no unrelated cleanup. The net-burden acceptance below keeps this honest.\n   - Constraint: behaviour is identical \u2014 meta/spec are unchanged; existing test expectations are not weakened.\n\n   Phase 0 \u2014 establish a test safety net (gate before any refactor).\n   A behaviour-preserving refactor is unverifiable without tests that would catch a behaviour change, so refactoring is gated on sufficient coverage:\n   - Assess existing coverage of the target's observable behaviour (tests that exercise the unit directly or transitively), judged against `{nominal, edge, boundary}` per the project Test formalism.\n   - If insufficient, add characterization tests capturing CURRENT observable behaviour (state/outputs, never interactions; per `testing-without-mocks`). Adding tests that document existing behaviour does not change behaviour or spec \u2014 it strengthens the proof.\n   - These tests must be GREEN against the unmodified code before any refactoring begins.\n   - If the unit cannot be characterized safely (e.g. an untestable side-effect tangle), the task records that finding and either (a) first introduces a minimal seam to make it testable, or (b) is closed with the finding (scope drift -> close per Munera). No refactor proceeds without a green net.\n\n   Phase 1 \u2014 refactor under the green net. Decomplect the target with minimal, local, root-cause changes (not superficial extraction).\n   Objective acceptance criteria:\n   - Burden reduction (A5 \u2014 named comparison source). Re-run `bb gordian local --json` from the worktree root and compare against the stored `munera/open/NNN-slug/before-local.json` captured in this step \u2014 that file is the single authoritative baseline for every \"decreased\" check (not the selector's emitted evidence, not a fresh pre-refactor recompute). The target unit's `lcc-total` (keyed by `(ns, var, arity, line)` \u2014 the same unique key the selector's join uses; `line` disambiguates same-named null-arity `defmethod` units that share `(ns, var, arity)`, e.g. the 51 `execute-effect!` defmethods) decreased versus its `before-local.json` value.\n   - Net burden (A2 \u2014 \"touched units\" defined). \"Touched units\" means every unit whose recomputed `lcc-total` changed between `before-local.json` and the after-`local` run \u2014 i.e. the set is computed from the metric, not from the diff/touched files. This deliberately includes callers whose `dependency`/`working-set` burden shifts even though their source was not edited, because `local` is recomputed globally. The acceptance is: summing `lcc-total` over this metric-derived touched set, the after total is strictly less than the before total, with each unit `u` identified by `(ns, var, arity, line)` (the selector's unique join key, so null-arity `defmethod` units do not collapse together): `{u | before(u) != after(u)}`, then `sum after < sum before`.\n   - Architectural no-regression (A3 \u2014 enforcing gate flags). Run `bb gordian gate --baseline munera/open/NNN-slug/before-diagnose.edn --fail-on new-cycles,new-high-findings --max-new-medium-findings 0`. The bare `gate --baseline` only EVALUATES checks; the `--fail-on` flag is what makes new cycles and new high findings FAIL (non-zero exit), and `--max-new-medium-findings 0` enforces the \"no new medium findings\" half of the claim. The gate must PASS (exit 0) with these flags.\n   - The Phase 0 characterization tests and all existing tests for the affected area are GREEN (same expectations as before the refactor).\n   - The change is minimal, local, and decomplecting.\n\n   Autonomy note: this generated task's design is intentionally authored autonomously (objective, narrow: fixed target + preserve behaviour + objective acceptance); the `task-lifecycle` `review-task-design` loop iterates ambiguity/architecture/inconsistency in place of live user collaboration.\n\n7. Commit the task creation on the current branch.\n   - Commit the new `munera/open/NNN-slug/` task directory (including both baseline files) on the current branch, so delegated lifecycle child sessions inherit the same worktree and can resolve the emitted task path.\n\n8. Emit a structured handoff as your final response.\n   - Output a compact Markdown summary with these headings exactly:\n     - `## Selection Outcome`\n     - `## Munera Task`\n     - `## Handoff Data`\n   - Under `## Selection Outcome`, summarize the chosen target and its evidence (ns/var/arity, file, line range, lcc-total, cc, gap), and the coverage hint.\n   - Under `## Munera Task`, give the task id/slug and the baselines captured.\n   - Under `## Handoff Data`, include this machine-friendly bullet line:\n     - `munera_task_path:` \u2014 the `munera/open/NNN-slug` task path.\n   - You may include `worktree_path:` as informational context, but downstream lifecycle execution must rely on inherited session worktree rather than calling `work-on`.\n   - If a field is not available, omit it rather than inventing it.
   - End the final response with exactly `PASS_STATUS: REVIEW_COMPLETE` so the workflow deterministically continues to the lifecycle step.\n\nExecution constraints:\n- Work only on the single chosen unit from the `incidental-complexity-finder` selection.\n- Prefer root-cause simplification framing over superficial extraction in the generated design.\n- Do NOT call `work-on`.\n- Do NOT create or switch worktrees.\n- Do NOT create a task when no unit qualifies.\n- Do NOT push or open a PR; this workflow ends with a completed, reviewed task on the current local branch (the user decides on PR).\n\nInput:\n{{input}}",
     :vars {"input" {:from :workflow-input}}}],
   :judge
   {:type :invoke,
    :operation "workflow/pass-status-routing",
    :args {:text {:from {:step "select-and-create" :output :final-llm-reply}},
           :allowed-statuses ["ACTIONABLE_FEEDBACK" "REVIEW_COMPLETE"]}},
   :on {"DONE" {:goto "lifecycle"},
        "REPEAT" {:goto :done}}}
  {:name "lifecycle",
   :type :delegate,
   :target "task-lifecycle",
   :prompt-string
   {:type :map,
    :fields {:input {:from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}}},
   :context
   [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}]}],
 :name "reduce-incidental-complexity",
 :description
 "Select the single highest incidental-complexity unit, open a constrained behaviour-preserving refactor task in the current worktree, and drive it through the full task lifecycle"}
